{title: Midnight in the Prison}
{subtitle: Acts 16:25–34}
{key: F}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [–] |
| [F] | [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] | ×4

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Down in the [F]dungeon, [C]feet in [Dm]the stocks
[Bb]Paul and [F]Silas [C]behind the [Dm]locks
[Bb]Around [F]midnight [C]they began [Dm]to pray
[Bb]Singing hymns [F]to God, [C]and the prisoners heard them [Dm]that day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]And the chains fell [F]loose, the [C]doors flew [Dm]open
[Bb]Every prison [F]shook, [C]every chain was [Dm]broken
[Bb]Sing at [F]midnight, [C]sing in the [Dm]night
[Bb]Till the [F]morning [C]comes with the [Dm]light
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] | [C] | ×2
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]The jailer [F]woke [C]and he drew [Dm]his sword
[Bb]Do not [F]harm yourself, [C]we are [Dm]all here, said [Bb]Paul
[F]What must I [C]do to be [Dm]saved, he [Bb]cried
Be[F]lieve in the Lord [C]Jesus and you'll [Dm]be saved, they replied
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]And the chains fell [F]loose, [C]the doors flew [Dm]open
[Bb]Every prison [F]shook, [C]every chain was [Dm]broken
[Bb]Sing at [F]midnight, [C]sing in the [Dm]night
[Bb]Till the [F]morning [C]comes with the [Dm]light
{end_of_chorus}

